llowing statements are true?\n\n- The equation $x_1\\mathbf{a}_1+x_2\\mathbf{a}_2+x_3\\mathbf{a}_3=\\mathbf{0}$ has an infinite number of nonzero solutions.\n\n- The vectors $\\mathbf{a}_1,\\mathbf{a}_2,$ and $\\mathbf{a}_3$ are linearly independent.\n\n- The vectors $\\mathbf{a}_1,\\mathbf{a}_2,$ and $\\mathbf{a}_3$ are linearly dependent." 13194139536181 true] [17592186119844 1020 #edb/ref 17592186387568 13194139536181 true] [17592186119844 1020 #edb/ref 17592186387575 13194139536181 true] [17592186119844 1020 #edb/ref 17592186387582 13194139536181 true] [17592186119844 1020 #edb/ref 17592186387624 13194139536181 true] [17592186119845 1020 #edb/ref 17592186387603 13194139536181 true] [17592186119845 1020 #edb/ref 17592186387610 13194139536181 true] [17592186119845 1020 #edb/ref 17592186387617 13194139536181 true] [17592186119846 1020 #edb/ref 17592186387589 13194139536181 true] [17592186119846 1020 #edb/ref 17592186387596 13194139536181 true] [17592186119846 1020 #edb/ref 17592186387631 13194139536181 true] [17592186387568 1017 #edb/ref 17592186387569 13194139536181 true] [17592186387568 1089 "q-105291" 13194139536181 true] [17592186387568 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139536181 true] [17592186387568 1100 "The set ${{a}_{1},{a}_{2}}$ is linearly dependent. Which of the following vectors could be ${a}_{2}$ if\n${a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}9 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]?$" 13194139536181 true] [17592186387568 1113 #uuid "faa7ddb4-5b88-5e56-a53e-35fdb9d2ef93" 13194139536181 true] [17592186387568 1145 "We say that two vectors ${v}_{1}$ and ${v}_{2}$ are *linearly independent* if the only solution to the equation\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{v}_{1}+{x}_{2}{v}_{2}=0\n$$\n\nis ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}=0.$ Otherwise, the vectors are *linearly dependent*.\n\nA set containing *only two* vectors is linearly *dependent* if and only if the two vectors are parallel.\n\nFrom the given options, the correct answer is \n\n$$\n{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTo see why, notice that \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]=\\frac{1}{3}[\\begin{aligned}9 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]=\\frac{1}{3}{a}_{1}.\n$$\n\nThis way, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{3}{a}_{1}-\\frac{1}{3}{a}_{1} & =0 \\\\ \\frac{1}{3}{a}_{1}-{a}_{2} & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn other words, the vectors ${a}_{1}$ and ${a}_{2}$ are parallel.\n\nTo see why this means that ${a}_{1}$ and ${a}_{2}$ are linearly dependent, we notice that the equation\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}=0\n$$\n\nhas the solution ${x}_{1}=\\frac{1}{3}$ and ${x}_{2}=-1,$ which is different from ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}=0.$ Therefore, the set is linearly dependent." 13194139536181 true] [17592186387569 1000 #edb/ref 17592186387570 13194139536181 true] [17592186387569 1000 #edb/ref 17592186387571 13194139536181 true] [17592186387569 1000 #edb/ref 17592186387572 13194139536181 true] [17592186387569 1000 #edb/ref 17592186387573 13194139536181 true] [17592186387569 1000 #edb/ref 17592186387574 13194139536181 true] [17592186387569 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139536181 true] [17592186387569 1041 "selection" 13194139536181 true] [17592186387569 1104 #edb/ref 17592186387573 13194139536181 true] [17592186387569 1110 #uuid "7fcc5fcb-b78f-537c-9052-00d024f08b3f" 13194139536181 true] [17592186387570 1034 "[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]" 13194139536181 true] [17592186387570 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536181 true] [17592186387570 1111 #uuid "7722ec08-e07e-5035-8463-5614f640ebc7" 13194139536181 true] [17592186387571 1034 "[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]" 13194139536181 true] [17592186387571 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536181 true] [17592186387571 1111 #uuid "8f0f1fe3-3b0a-5643-8234-d64b88e8e8ca" 13194139536181 true] [17592186387572 1034 "[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]" 13194139536181 true] [17592186387572 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536181 true] [17592186387572 1111 #uuid "75c3e248-a555-55be-94ce-d9ab0f9e5912" 13194139536181 true] [17592186387573 103