39536181 true] [17592186387582 1100 "The set ${{a}_{1},{a}_{2}}$ is linearly dependent. Which of the following vectors could be ${a}_{2}$ if\n${a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]?$" 13194139536181 true] [17592186387582 1113 #uuid "582f634c-02c7-58e7-9850-c7663e72a87b" 13194139536181 true] [17592186387582 1145 "We say that two vectors ${v}_{1}$ and ${v}_{2}$ are *linearly independent* if the only solution to the equation\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{v}_{1}+{x}_{2}{v}_{2}=0\n$$\n\nis ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}=0.$ Otherwise, the vectors are *linearly dependent*.\n\nA set containing *only two* vectors is linearly *dependent* if and only if the two vectors are parallel.\n\nFrom the given options, the correct answer is \n\n$$\n{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}-10 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTo see why, notice that \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}-10 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]=(-2)[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]=-2{a}_{1}.\n$$\n\nThis way, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{a}_{1}-2{a}_{1} & =0 \\\\ 2{a}_{1}+{a}_{2} & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn other words, the vectors ${a}_{1}$ and ${a}_{2}$ are parallel.\n\nTo see why this means that ${a}_{1}$ and ${a}_{2}$ are linearly dependent, we notice that the equation\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}=0\n$$\n\nhas the solution ${x}_{1}=2$ and ${x}_{2}=1,$ which is different from ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}=0.$ Therefore, the set is linearly dependent." 13194139536181 true] [17592186387583 1000 #edb/ref 17592186387584 13194139536181 true] [17592186387583 1000 #edb/ref 17592186387585 13194139536181 true] [17592186387583 1000 #edb/ref 17592186387586 13194139536181 true] [17592186387583 1000 #edb/ref 17592186387587 13194139536181 true] [17592186387583 1000 #edb/ref 17592186387588 13194139536181 true] [17592186387583 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139536181 true] [17592186387583 1041 "selection" 13194139536181 true] [17592186387583 1104 #edb/ref 17592186387587 13194139536181 true] [17592186387583 1110 #uuid "e0714d41-23bd-5117-80