g *only two* vectors is linearly *dependent* if and only if the two vectors are parallel.\n\nFrom the given options, the correct answer is\n\n$$\n{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTo see why, notice that \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}]=-\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -6 \\\\ 8\\end{aligned}]=-\\frac{1}{2}{a}_{1}.\n$$\n\nThis way, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2}{a}_{1}-\\frac{1}{2}{a}_{1} & =0 \\\\ \\frac{1}{2}{a}_{1}+{a}_{2} & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn other words, the vectors ${a}_{1}$ and ${a}_{2}$ are parallel.\n\nTo see why this means that ${a}_{1}$ and ${a}_{2}$ are linearly dependent, we notice that the equation\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}=0\n$$\n\nhas the solution ${x}_{1}=\\frac{1}{2}$ and ${x}_{2}=1,$ which is different from ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}=0.$ Therefore, the set is linearly dependent." 13194139536181 true] [17592186387625 1000 #edb/ref 17592186387626 13194139536181 true] [17592186387625 1000 #edb/ref 17592186387627 13194139536181 true] [17592186387625 1000 #edb/ref 17592186387628 13194139536181 true] [17592186387625 1000 #edb/ref 17592186387629 13194139536181 true] [17592186387625 1000 #edb/ref 17592186387630 13194139536181 true] [17592186387625 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139536181 true] [17592186387625 1041 "selection" 13194139536181 true] [17592186387625 1104 #edb/ref 17592186387626 13194139536181 true] [17592186387625 1110 #uuid "cfeb2459-8c66-5226-a8f8-5fcedfc43e89" 13194139536181 true] [17592186387626 1034 "[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}]" 13194139536181 true] [17592186387626 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536181 true] [17592186387626 1111 #uuid "d2819f39-f4ce-5ff7-ae4b-99356cd2abb6" 13194139536181 true] [17592186387627 1034 "[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ -10 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]" 13194139536181 true] [17592186387627 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536181 true] [17592186387627 1111 #uuid "40236b2e-fa08-5071-99d2-4a8c1ed178a8" 131941395