ements.\n\nThe equation ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3}=0$ corresponds to the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-2{x}_{2}+3{x}_{3}=0 \\\\ {x}_{2}-{x}_{3}=0 \\\\ -3{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}-4{x}_{3}=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo solve the system, we create its augmented matrix and reduce it using Gaussian elimination:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 1 & -4 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -5 & 5 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+5{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the matrix above, we conclude that the basic variables are ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$, while ${x}_{3}$ is the free variable. \n\nSince there is one free variable, the equation ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3}=0$ has an infinite number of nonzero solutions, which means that the vectors are linearly dependent. \n\nTherefore, statements I and II are false, while statement III is true." 13194139536181 true] [17592186387632 1000 #edb/ref 17592186387633 13194139536181 true] [17592186387632 1000 #edb/ref 17592186387634 13194139536181 true] [17592186387632 1000 #edb/ref 17592186387635 13194139536181 true] [17592186387632 1000 #edb/ref 17592186387636 13194139536181 true] [17592186387632 1000 #edb/ref 17592186387637 13194139536181 true] [17592186387632 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139536181 true] [17592186387632 1041 "selection" 13194139536181 true] [17592186387632 1104 #edb/ref 17592186387635 13194139536181 true] [17592186387632 1110 #uuid "529d64d1-0dba-5819-ae1f-c03df83356b6" 13194139536181 true] [17592186387633 1034 "None of the statements are true" 13194139536181 true] [17592186387633 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139536181 true] [17592186387633 1111 #uuid "6af199a0-7219-5771-addc-80944cbe9fb8" 13194139536181 true] [17592186387634 1034 "I and III 